Z||000000||underdog||07-08-2001||03:48 PM||||ok i know you are all probablt tired of this question but i really need help<P><BR>can an engine (2.8) from a mid 80s camaro/firebird go in my 86 gt? or are they different engines than ours?<P>my engine is basically dead. i want a knew one but cheap. i can get the 2.8 camaro engines pretty redialy but fieros and especially their engines are hard to come by.<P><BR>please list all info you have, or if there is an easier swap, say a 3800 or something, anything, please tell me<P>thanks<P>oh by the way im gonna keep bringing this up until i have a new engine, so get your info iin fast to stop my redundantness...ha ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||07-08-2001||03:56 PM||||No , The starter is on the wrong side. And for the time it takes to swap in a 2.8 from an Fbody , which I believe is 20hp less than a std fiero v6 , you could swap in a much much better motor.<P>I was looking throught he local buy and sell today , I saw 3 Caddy 4.5 4.9ltr V8's for sale for under $200 all running , all said good condition. 3800 series ones are just as cheap.<P>If your going to all the trouble , do something with some power<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||underdog||07-08-2001||04:44 PM||||thats what i think too<P>ok, now what is a really easy swap then? i need the engine and i imagine the tranny no? what engines can i just drop in?||||reg||6
Z||000003||KRMFiero||07-08-2001||05:44 PM|||| <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx</A> <P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 Project<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>       <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> <BR>AOL: Physcokyle||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||07-08-2001||08:39 PM||||A word of caution.  No non Fiero engine swap is as straight forward as some tend to indicate.  Those who have done swaps in the past have the experience and understand what needs to be done.  Swaping 3800's , norstars, or other V8s call for a lot of wiring modifications, including ECM change.  Cheap won't make the grade for the swap.  Ease of swap a Fiero 2.8, built up if you want, but not cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||07-08-2001||11:38 PM||||You can swap a Camaro 3.4 just as easily as a Camaro 2.8.<P>If you want a drop in swap, pull a 3.1 out of a Lumina or something similar.||||reg||1
Z||000006||underdog||07-09-2001||02:50 AM||||thanks guys, any other input?||||reg||10
Z||000007||Raydar||07-09-2001||03:22 AM||||I would recommend the 3.1 Lumina minivan engine. Ed Parks used to do these before he started doing 3.4 Camaro motors. <BR>The Fiero intake system and ignition will bolt straight on. <BR>The 3.1 in the Lumina passenger car (at least the ones I've seen) is a Gen II. Uses different heads and accessory mounting points. Also is a DIS (crank-trigger ignition) system. Will require that the ECM from the donor be transplanted as well. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Doni Hagan||07-09-2001||12:05 PM||||Is there any particular year minivan to look for or are they all the same engine? I bet I can find one pretty cheap. ||||reg||6
Z||000009||Raydar||07-09-2001||03:24 PM||||Just the "iron head" version. If it's got a distributor, you should be okay. Don't know what years, though.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
